CM_ BO_ 576 "Canonical ECU accumulator temperatures and SoC, mirrored byte-for-byte from Telemetry CAN at 10 Hz. TTCS consumes the mapped maximum; raw 32767 is invalid. TTCS requires a new frame within 500 ms. Summary fallback provides no minimum.";
BA_ "GenMsgCycleTime" BO_ 576 100;
BA_ "GenMsgSendType" BO_ 576 0;

CM_ SG_ 576 ECU_AccuTempMax "Canonical car accumulator maximum, converted by ECU using voltage recovery and Table 5. Prefer complete fresh sweeps; if no sweep frames are fresh, use a fresh mapped summary maximum (1 degC input resolution). Partial or invalid live sweeps prevent fallback. 0x7FFF is invalid. Identical ECU_DashData bytes reach TTCS on Control CAN and screen on Telemetry/Dash CAN.";

CM_ SG_ 576 ECU_AccuTempMin "Corrected minimum from complete fresh sensor sweeps. 0x7FFF is invalid, including during summary-maximum fallback; summary supplies no minimum.";

CM_ BO_ 1760 "MUR ADDITION (PROVISIONAL, bench/demo): parameter-storage request endpoint for node 0, ID 0x6E0 + node. Classic-CAN ISO-TP: this frame is one 8-byte fragment (ISO-TP PCI byte + 7 data bytes), reassembled by the parameter service; telemetry must not treat the bytes as signals. Reserved block 0x6E0-0x6E7 requests, 0x6E8-0x6EF responses; canboot uses 0x7E0/0x7E8. ISO-TP flow control for a request arrives on 0x6E8 + node. Wire format, catalog and validation: generated/params/mur_params.h and mur_msgs.params. No parameter signal is finalized and no proto exists.";
CM_ BO_ 1768 "MUR ADDITION (PROVISIONAL, bench/demo): parameter-storage response endpoint for node 0, ID 0x6E8 + node. ISO-TP fragment of the shared 16-byte header plus at most 4096 payload bytes; see PARAM_Request and generated/params/mur_params.h. Never decoded as a signal.";
CM_ BO_ 1761 "MUR ADDITION (PRODUCTION TTCS): parameter-storage request endpoint for node 1 (ttcs_control) on Control CAN, ID 0x6E1. ISO-TP fragment of the shared 16-byte header plus at most 4096 payload bytes; carries the 108-element ttcs_r0_prior (ID 256). Never decoded as a signal.";
CM_ BO_ 1769 "MUR ADDITION (PRODUCTION TTCS): parameter-storage response endpoint for node 1 (ttcs_control) on Control CAN, ID 0x6E9. Same fragment layout as PARAM_Response; see generated/params/mur_params.h. Never decoded as a signal.";
BA_ "GenMsgSendType" BO_ 1760 2;
BA_ "GenMsgSendType" BO_ 1768 2;
